        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 80-year-old male patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Spirometry supported the underlying obstructive pattern. He was promptly initiated on supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, and a course of systemic corticosteroids administered intravenously. Blood tests were obtained to exclude secondary complications. The patient responded satisfactorily to treatment with improvement in respiratory function and oxygenation. He is discharged in stable condition with optimised inhaler therapy and a short oral steroid taper. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
